  "subject": "a man who misreads grams in a curry recipe, cooks a five-kilo pot, and has to eat it for seven days, reinventing it each night as curry udon, curry toast, curry fried rice and curry hotpot",
  "caption": "Mandarin pop on a New Orleans second-line brass band groove. Punchy trumpet riffs, smeared trombone slides, bouncing sousaphone bass line, syncopated second-line snare with bass drum and cymbal. Loose live street-band sound. Male baritone lead vocal, hearty and clearly sung, with gang vocal shout-backs on the chorus. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 104 BPM, B-flat major. Rowdy kitchen comedy. No trap, no autotune, no rap, no EDM, no smooth jazz.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro - sousaphone, second-line snare, trumpet riff]\n\n[Verse 1]\n食譜寫五百克\n我看成五公斤\n鍋子裝到滿出來\n整個家都是咖哩\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n星期一 白飯\n星期二 烏龍麵\n\n[Chorus]\n咖哩第七天 還沒吃完\n加起司 加雞蛋 換個樣子\n咖哩第七天 我不投降\n鍋底還有 一大半\n\n[Verse 2]\n星期三 夾吐司\n星期四 炒成飯\n星期五 加高湯\n煮成一鍋火鍋\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n朋友一聞到味道\n就知道我來了\n\n[Chorus]\n咖哩第七天 終於見底\n刮一刮 鍋邊 最後一口\n咖哩第七天 白飯我想你\n明天配醬油就好\n\n[Outro - brass shout chorus, drums]\n下次食譜 我要看兩遍",
